  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "spraying; atomizing; misting",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "spraying; atomizing; misting",
      "explanation": "The act of dispersing a liquid as a fine mist or spray. Used for agricultural spraying, medical applications, cleaning products, and similar contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21104_funmu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{消毒液|しょうどくえき}を{噴霧|ふんむ}する。",
      "english": "To spray disinfectant.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21104_funmu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{農薬|のうやく}の{噴霧|ふんむ}は{風|かぜ}のない{日|ひ}に{行|おこな}う。",
      "english": "Pesticide spraying is done on windless days.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21104_funmu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{暑|あつ}い{日|ひ}に{公園|こうえん}でミストを{噴霧|ふんむ}して、{涼|すず}しさを{提供|ていきょう}するサービスがある。",
      "english": "On hot days, there are services that spray mist in parks to provide cooling.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Describes the dispersal of liquid as a fine mist or spray. Used in agriculture (pesticide spraying), medical settings (disinfection), cosmetics, and cooling systems.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {噴霧|ふんむ}する: to spray, to atomize\n- {噴霧器|ふんむき}: sprayer, atomizer\n- {噴霧|ふんむ}{消毒|しょうどく}: spray disinfection\n- {噴霧|ふんむ}{式|しき}: spray-type\n- {噴霧|ふんむ}ノズル: spray nozzle\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- スプレー: spray — the loanword equivalent; more casual and everyday\n- {散布|さんぷ}: scattering, spraying — broader; can include spreading seeds or distributing leaflets, not just liquid\n- {霧吹|きりふ}き: spray bottle, mister — refers to the handheld tool itself\n\nETYMOLOGY:\n{噴|ふん} (spout, emit) + {霧|む} (mist, fog) — \"emit mist.\"",
